[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Class 0 Telematics Security Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @vcr_grammar

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This section specifies cybersecurity requirements for Class 0 vehicle systems: **Telematics, Fleet Management Information Systems (FMIS), and Electronic Logging Devices (ELDs)**. Class 0 telematics systems are distributed systems; the *Telematics Systems in Commercial Fleets: Special Handling & Evaluation Guidance* section of the overview describes their components and the VCR requirement sets that cover them.

Instructions for Preparing and Responding to Questionnaires:
============================================================
- **Evaluate All Telematics Systems**: A single tractor or trailer may incorporate multiple telematics systems (e.g., OEM factory gateway, aftermarket ELD/FMIS, powertrain telematics, camera/vision safety subsystems). A complete vehicle assessment requires separate responses for **each** distinct telematics system present.
- **Connectivity Worksheet**: The supplier questionnaire provides a dedicated *Class 0 - Connectivity* worksheet for the Class 0 wireless interfaces.
- **CLOUD and MOBILE Questionnaires**: Evaluate applicable CLOUD services and MOBILE software using their respective questionnaires, including when those services or software interface with devices outside Class 0.
- **Distributed Responsibilities**: OEMs, suppliers, and procurement teams should route each questionnaire to the responsible engineering and operations teams.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Wireless Connectivity Security Requirements Applicability

